    "narrative": "Our highest confidence play today is **Corbin Carroll**, who leads the team with a robust 80.77 score. He faces Andrew Abbott, and despite the inherent platoon disadvantage against a southpaw, the combination of a favorable park and a high-upside order spot makes him the engine of our offense. Similarly, **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) is positioned for a strong day against Waguespack. His dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) against a righty, paired with the stability of hitting third, makes him a foundational piece for our Roto points today. **Gabriel Moreno** (66.77) and **Henry Bolte** (60.79) also clear our threshold comfortably, benefiting from favorable matchups against softer pitching, with **Henry Bolte** specifically gaining significant leverage from his leadoff spot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was undoubtedly **Isaac Paredes**, who finished just outside the starting nine with a 45.78 score. While his pedigree is strong, his matchup against Basso presented a \"Dynamic Platoon\" penalty (-9%) that suppressed his overall efficiency relative to the rest of the utility mix. We opted to prioritize **Mickey Moniak** (54.50) and **Jose Caballero** (46.26) for their park-adjusted profiles and positional versatility, despite the latter struggling with a late-order hit spot. We continue to monitor the status of **James Wood**, who remains sidelined on the IL, leaving us to navigate a crowded outfield without his production.\n\nManagers should remain alert to the risk profiles of our lower-score starters. **Austin Riley** (48.83) and **Seiya Suzuki** (49.48) are functioning near our marginal floor today due to difficult matchups against elite or high-efficiency arms like Drohan and Miller. While **Seiya Suzuki** receives a slight efficiency bump for facing a pitcher with a slow delivery\u2014enhancing his stolen base potential\u2014the overall ceiling for both remains dampened by park factors and opponent skill. Ensure that bench depth options like **Griffin Conine** or **Cole Young** are ready to rotate in if late-breaking lineup changes or adverse weather shift the projections further.",
